# Docs and git

- **Markdown → Word**: On Windows/PowerShell, refresh PATH if needed after installing Pandoc, then run `pandoc` from `docs/` (e.g. `--toc --toc-depth=2 -s`). Report success, path, and file size when verifying exports.
- **Diagrams in docs**: Prefer simple, legible diagrams (readable labels, consistent direction) when converting MD to docx — Pandoc can mangle complex Mermaid; simplify or use static images when readability suffers.
- **Branches**: Feature work has used names like **`dev_MVP_423`**; keep branch names and commit messages clear and match team conventions when the user requests git operations.
- **Office Timeline exports**: Office Timeline imports CSV with the columns **task name, start, finish**. Encode milestones as rows where **start == finish**. Project timeline CSVs live under `pricing_ab_test/timeline/`; match that location and column shape so the file opens cleanly in Office Timeline without remapping.
